{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat tools/p11/README.md docs/planning/refinements/2026-11-04/execution.md; git diff f1e58da5cdeb1c67eed650b186081661cefc2fa2 --stat'","aggregated_output":"# Shared P11 qualification and actual reviews\n\nThe accepted D063 plan selects the changed C46–C49 flows. P09/P10 and RC1 retain\ntheir original results and artifacts. One actual P11 Check/Test run and fixture\ncandidate serve all four chunk reviews and the phase review. No phase run is\ncopied, renamed or reported as a newly executed chunk run. The standard ledger\nremains unchanged (`controller_complete:false`), as with the accepted P10 manual\nreview fallback.\n\nUse the existing Rust Runner's registered P11 focused command plans and one\n`xtask native-prepare --phase P11 --target aarch64-apple-darwin --features\ntest-fixtures`. Finish source preflight before that build. Real source failures\nget causal checks; driver-only fixes retain the same verified app bytes. Keep\nall failed attempts. Do not rerun unrelated Rust/native suites for provenance.\n\n`acceptance_p11.py` requires the explicit fixture bundle, owned processes and\nlocal synthetic endpoints. It records measured facts and capture hashes first.\nIts no-UI finalizer requires an actual source-bound P11 test RunRecord and an\nexplicit, capture-specific visual review. No pixels or invisible authority\nboundary are inferred from a test count, successful script exit or AX absence.\n\n`proof.py make` binds the actual Check/Test RunRecords, current metadata-only\nfingerprint, prepare, finalized native record, original observation manifest and\nbuild receipt into one immutable qualification folder. Its CLI lists the exact\nrequired inputs. It reuses P10's raw evidence validator and rejects missing or\nchanged command/native membership, logs, current source/dependencies, candidate,\nhelpers, incomplete build inputs and failed observation exits. The Python source\nhash recomputation was checked against the actual Rust fingerprint algorithm.\n\nFor the two reviewed conditional-style fixes, `--check` may name an explicit\n`airs-desktop/p11-check-selection/1` receipt. It binds the original failed Check\nrun, exact before/current source inventories, the fixed module's exact hashes,\nand a current `airs-desktop/p11-check-supplement/1` containing only affected or\npreviously blocked commands. Every registered command is accounted in order.\nPassing setup/bindings/typecheck/compile results may be `carried_unaffected`\nwith a reason; their original source, timestamps and logs remain bound. Format\nand all affected/blocked lint/notice checks execute. This receipt is never a\nnew passing full-run record. Tests and native assertions still execute on the\nshared current candidate, and archived standing uses this same strict consumer.\nThe dated test-only `unwrap` to descriptive `expect` correction is also bound\nby its exact old/new hashes. `airs-desktop/rust-test-build-carry/1` retains the\noriginal build/prepare and binds the current Check selection and Test run; only\nthat Rust test file may differ. It requires no frontend or native rebuild and\ndoes not claim either was executed. Executable and complete bundle verification\nremain independent requirements.\n\nFor a frontend test-only source change, `--build-input-carry` requires the\noriginal native build and a successful current-source frontend rebuild whose\ncomplete output is byte-identical. Its command, input hashes and raw log remain\nbound; the retained native build is never reported as newly executed.\n\n`review.py make C46 attempt-01 QUALIFICATION` (likewise C47–C49) writes a frozen\nrequest and inventories. Launch it with the retained\n`tools/p09/launch-remedial-review.py C46 attempt-01 gpt-6.1-sol`, then use\n`review.py audit C46 attempt-01`. The launcher requests a fresh, ephemeral,\nread-only reviewer with hooks/plugins/network/UI features disabled. Every actual\nscore and finding is retained. After all four pass the full gate, make and audit\nthe P11 request against exactly the same qualification. Chunk acceptance at8\nfollows D034; P11 still requires every member and phase at9 with empty findings.\n\n`standing.finalize(root, qualification, attempts)` runs only after those five\nactual reviews. It refuses existing outputs, verifies the three explicit LFS\npaths, and archives the exact source, fixture app and proof/evidence membership.\n`standing.py release-prerequisites` subsequently verifies that archived standing\nwithout a current `target` directory, installed app, host toolchain or matching\nhostname. Production promotion requires both the original P09/P10 proof and this\nnew P11 standing. Stable installed/live acceptance and Linux qualification remain\nseparate. These tools perform no signing, publication or live product calls.\n\n## VM affected verification after the Modal fix\n\nThe dedicated VM uses the unchanged registered command plan. Run selected labels\nwith the existing Runner through the small build-only example:\n\n    cargo run --locked -p xtask --example p11_affected -- check C46/check/1 C46/check/4\n    cargo run --locked -p xtask --example p11_affected -- test <all 12 registered frontend labels, in order>\n\nThis produces ordinary subset RunRecords. It refuses setup, unknown, duplicate\nand reordered labels; it does not create full-suite or controller completion.\nThe source checks originally run on Kirk retain their original logs and inputs.\n\nThe optional proof.py make --impact-selection FILE keeps --check and --tests\npointing to the original D2 records. FILE has schema\nairs-desktop/p11-impact-selection/1, current runner_inputs, a nonempty reason,\nand these bound references: baseline_source, baseline_candidate,\nbaseline_check, baseline_test, current_source, tool_transition, and\ncurrent_runs (check/test). Both source records contain files and git_config.\nIt also lists exact changed_paths, dependencies from carry_dependencies,\nand affected labels: the two checks above and all registered frontend tests.\n\nD2 is source-check context, with no native qualification claimed. Its permanent\narchive is docs/planning/evidence/P11/source-history/D2. The original failed\nCheck and its two repairs stay intact. Current format/typecheck and frontend\nresults execute in the VM; eight unchanged Rust test commands and seven other\nchecks are carried with explicit reasons. Dependencies include all desktop-core,\nxtask library, contracts, resources, architecture inputs and root lock/toolchain\nfiles. The tool audit must bind exact original/current compiler, Cargo, Node and\npnpm bytes; only the rustup shims may differ. No whole dependency hash is relabelled.\n\nThe P11 wrapper validates Check provenance at its original source context. The\nunchanged P10 generic consumer validates carried Rust results against their\noriginal candidate, raw runs/logs and exact dependency proofs. Every registered\nrequirement remains present. Final standing includes both source contexts and\nverifies without a target directory or the original host. A changed production\ndependency, omitted command, failed/zero-test result or changed compiler fails\nthe consumer. New native assertions still require actual current VM evidence.\n\n## Native helper continuation without replaying source QA\n\nFor helper/proof-only fixes after the VM source checks, --helper-source-carry\nbinds schema airs-desktop/p11-helper-source-carry/1. It names baseline_source\n(the archived S2 source seal), baseline_candidate (S2 app/VM context),\nimpact_selection (the original D2/S2 selection), current_source (S3), exact\nchanged_paths, current runner_inputs, unchanged conditions, a reason and qa refs.\nThe complete application input identities and dependency/build fingerprints must\nmatch. Only native/P11 helpers, their build-only example and owner execution\ndocumentation/attributes may change; an application edit is rejected.\n\nEach QA ref has schema airs-desktop/p11-helper-qa/1, actual argv/cwd, exit_code,\npositive passing tests, a bound log and helper_files mapping names to current\nhashes. The records must cover every changed Python helper. Their relevant\nhelper hashes bind validity; unrelated source edits do not force repeated QA.\n\nThe fourteen S2 frontend/check results retain their actual RunRecords and become\nreused_exact against the same app, flags and VM conditions with empty helper\ndependencies. The eight D2 Rust results remain carried_unaffected. Original\nfailed Check evidence stays unchanged. Both D2 and S2 source archives are in\nthe durable historical context; no current target or original host is needed.\n\nA native continuation names a native-selection/1 manifest and finalized standard\nacceptance. Per-row origins retain the failed original process status separately\nfrom completed assertion status. C46 uses its original completed observations\nand unchanged relevant helpers; remaining rows use the successful continuation.\nThe native provenance validator binds actual per-row logs, arguments, times,\ncapture reviews and app identities. A failed whole process is never relabelled\nas a newly passing process.\n\n### Review remediation without replaying unaffected flows\n\n`remediation.py RECEIPT --out FRESH_FOLDER` consumes the dated C46/C47/C48\nreview fixes. `proof.py verify FRESH_FOLDER/qualification.json` remains the\nreview entrypoint. This path preserves qualification02 and all original raw\noutcomes; it does not turn a failed contributing process into a passing run.\n\nThe receipt (`airs-desktop/p11-review-remediation/1`) binds the original\nqualification, D2/S2/S3 source history, the preserved original app tar, current\nsource/fingerprint/build/prepare, the actual nine Rust integration consumers,\nC48 source selectors, the old-artifact drawer-scroll supplement, current-artifact\nrecovery, helper QA, and a reason for every carried requirement. Exactly four\nfrontend files and two Rust fixture files have pinned before/after hashes. Other\napplication, dependency, native-helper or VM changes cannot silently use this\nreview decision. The versioned native build example is a build tool, not a\nproduction-source exemption.\n\nUnchanged rows retain their original result and candidate references. Explicit\n`carried_unaffected` dependency proofs include every resource and the relevant\nnative helpers. Source selectors replace only affected verification goals;\nthe original registered command remains visible. These custom selector records\nretain actual commands, logs, source inputs and known timing limitations rather\nthan manufacturing a complete `airs-v2/run/1` or claiming a whole command reran.\nC48's new recovery slice retains unrelated first-use/save facts as old subfact\norigins. It never presents the original 099/eb9 artifact as the new app.\n\nHistorical finalization archives the accepted source/app and retains all three\nprior source contexts. P10's generic coverage and historical consumers are\nunchanged. This path does not assign review scores or complete a controller.\n# Refinement qualification checkpoint — 2026-11-04\n\nCheckpoint: 2026-11-04 21:50 UTC. The current fixture build05 and its affected\nrecovery-native slice have passed. Recovery02 exited 0 with all ten facts true;\nall three captures were individually accepted. Qualification02 remains the\noriginal qualified 099/eb9 artifact. This evidence-before-seal checkpoint supplies the dated remediation consumer;\nits resulting bound qualification is authoritative for review admission. No\nunreturned review score or final P11 standing is claimed.\n\nThe owner-approved 17-item scope and decisions are in [plan.md](plan.md).\nAll development, local checks/builds and native UI run inside `admin@worf-vm`,\nbranch `refinement/20261104-vm`; Kirk's old native launcher is retired. The\nintegration base remains Forgejo main `f1e58da5cdeb1c67eed650b186081661cefc2fa2`.\n\n## Actual first reviews and focused remediations\n\nThese are the real attempt-01 scores, in architecture / behavior /\nauthority_security / validation / overall order. Raw verdicts, audited receipts,\nfindings and limitations remain unchanged. No scores were overridden.\n\n| Stream | Actual scores | Finding and focused follow-up |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| C46 | 9 / 9 / 9 / 8 / 8 | Older Harness/Inbox integration fixtures completed unauthenticated OAuth drafts and were omitted from affected coverage. Only the two test fixture files changed: authenticate synthetic credentials, reacquire context and assert completable. The nine named consumers passed (3 Harness + 6 Inbox); both targets' scoped Clippy passed. Production authentication gates are unchanged. |\n| C47 | 9 / 9 / 9 / 8 / 8 | Independent Explain scrolling lacked a native observation. A focused supplement on the exact original 099/eb9 app passed in 14 seconds: 11 fixture calls overflowed, lower call index4 was reached, drawer content moved and the underlying page anchor stayed fixed. Both images were individually accepted; fixture state, modes and trust roots stayed unchanged. |\n| C48 | 9 / 8 / 9 / 8 / 8 | A failed preferred-collection restore lost its warning/Retry after Home and back. Recovery now lives in scoped transient store state, observed before App snapshots render, with generation/action guards and explicit successful-choice retirement. Four production-path recovery tests and final typecheck passed. Actual earlier API 42, shell 29/Test Cases 16 and Save/Send 20 retain their exact earlier source bindings; bounded later recovery/message deltas are separately captured and tested. |\n| C49 | 9 / 9 / 9 / 9 / 9 | Full gate passed with no findings on qualification02. This historical verdict is not a new review of build05. |\n\nC46, C47 and C48 are accepted at eight under D034, with their actual full gates\nstill false and the push to nine open. Their acceptance records retain all open\nfindings. Every attempt-01 source/transport/qualification audit passed; the source\nstayed frozen throughout those reviews. The P11 phase review has not run.\n\nDurable focused records:\n\n- [C46 nine consumers and original red failures](../../evidence/P11/c46-consumer-remediation-01/manifest.json), plus [scoped target Clippy](../../evidence/P11/c46-consumer-remediation-01/clippy-supplement.json).\n- [C47 independent-scroll supplement](../../evidence/P11/c47-scroll-supplement-01/supplement.json), with original process/source and exact old-artifact bindings.\n- [C48 final and retained source selectors](../../evidence/P11/retained-qa/c48-recovery-02/supplement.json), including original failures, exact input snapshots and honest missing per-command UTC timing limitations.\n- [Versioned build helper Clippy/preflight](../../evidence/P11/native-candidate-adapter-01/manifest.json), [affected Rust formatting](../../evidence/P11/remediation-format-01/record.json), and [combined helper QA 81/81](../../evidence/P11/helper-qa-remediation-01/record.json).\n\nThe 81-test helper record retains its original consumer-source bindings. A\n[one-test parser follow-up](../../evidence/P11/helper-parser-followup-01/record.json)\nthen passed: extra actual recovery observations are retained, while every\nmandatory fact and every recorded value must pass. Missing/false facts, foreign\nartifacts/VM/helpers, unreviewed captures and reversed times still reject. The\n81 tests are not relabelled as a new execution after that narrow parser change.\n\n## Current candidate and remaining native slice\n\nThe one actual [VM build05](../../evidence/P11/native-build-05-vm/receipt.json)\ncompleted in 1 minute44 seconds. It used source commit\n`685e645366069b505e47e375693689ac3db573fa` plus the separately frozen evidence\nconsumer work. All 660 application input identities stayed fixed through the\nbuild. The executable SHA256 is\n`ba72d82de279be8d311c02125597ae0d5d6f7f5f0f2bdcbc2d951dc3d1e42914`;\nthe complete bundle SHA256 is\n`f558aa269e359e9617191ecd47b8eb63016350086e618c36c4fdfc79d45bd535`.\nIts [versioned preparation](../../evidence/P11/native-build-05-vm/native-prepare.json)\nuses the same fixed ARM64 fixture recipe. The sealed canonical old prepare was\nnot overwritten. The exact old 099 app survives as a verified CoW snapshot and\n[public tar payload](../../evidence/P11/remediation-baseline-01/receipt.json).\n\nRecovery01 stopped **before assertions** because the new ad-hoc-signed app could\nnot read its existing synthetic fixture encryption key. Metadata showed that\nitem trusted only the older code signature. That failed attempt remains failed.\nThe exact-item fixture repair appended only the new code requirement, retaining\nthe old trusted application, item value, attributes and other ACLs. The GUI\nhelper's persistent SetAccess succeeded, then its CoreFoundation object-equality\npostcheck failed; its exit1 is preserved. An independent, read-only exact\nmetadata validator proves the append and every other before/after byte unchanged.\nThe [transition receipt](../../evidence/P11/fixture-code-access-verification-01/receipt.json)\nand [validator receipt](../../evidence/P11/fixture-code-access-verification-01/validator-receipt.json)\nrecord this distinction. Owner GO authorized the exact synthetic dialog and\nscreen-access renewal; only the public fixture password was entered. No owner\npassword or credential value was read, and no default/login Keychain was touched.\nNo application rebuild followed this admission repair.\n\n[Recovery02](../../evidence/P11/recovery-native-02/supplement.json) actually ran\n21:46:00–21:46:43 UTC and exited 0. All ten facts passed: missing and replaced\nroot warnings survive Home/back; Retry is explicit and recovers once the root\nor identity is restored; intentional close survives restart; the original owned\ncollection is reopened; no request is replayed. All 660 application inputs and\nthe full native helper closure stayed unchanged. The fixture state JSON stayed\nbyte-identical and no endpoint requests were sent. Root individually inspected\nall three capture references; the two generic missing/replaced-warning PNGs are\nbyte-identical captures from separate actual states.\n\nThe raw picker-override-restored flag remains false because its helper comparison\nincluded an extra trailing newline. The separate\n[picker cleanup receipt](../../evidence/P11/recovery-native-02/picker-cleanup.json)\nproves the original override bytes were restored exactly afterward. No raw\nobservation or failure flag was rewritten. These are affected native observations,\nnot a replay of the other eleven assertions or of the entire original N03 flow.\n\n## Explicit reuse and original qualification\n\nThe dated remediation proof pins the exact old/new source hashes for four\nfrontend files and two Rust fixture files. It accounts for **35 unaffected\nrequirements** with per-ID rationale and conservative unchanged dependency\nidentities, including all resources and relevant native helpers. It retains\noriginal result/candidate/process references; changed executable bytes are not\ncalled byte-identical. Affected source selectors, formatting and recovery are\nseparate actual executions. The six new adversarial consumer tests are included\nin the 81/81 combined Python checks; no app/Rust/Node/native suite was executed by\nthat helper QA.\n\nThe original [qualification02](../../evidence/P11/qualification-final-02/qualification.json)\naccounts for all 41 registered requirements on its original 099/eb9 context.\nIts seven actual native origins, attempts06–12, supply all 12 positive assertions.\nFailed contributing process exits remain failed; attempt10's false keyboard\nfact remains explicitly excluded, replaced by attempt11's two genuine 56-Tab\ntraces and retained sixteen-layout matrix. Original source/evidence seals stay\nunchanged. D2, S2 and the exact [S3 archive](../../evidence/P11/remediation-baseline-01/source-S3-archive.json)\nmake those old source bindings independently reconstructible.\n\nOriginal VM source verification had 379 passing frontend tests. The original\ncomplete Kirk source Test run had 439 passing executions; its eight unchanged\nRust commands (62 executions) retain their original host/source/tool bindings.\nThe later build04 099/eb9 included the real Modal composition/focus fix and the\nAdministration test correction. Those results were not relabelled as new VM or\nbuild05 executions.\n\nThe old warning-history visibility supplement, original dated reason, latest\nPassed/resolved timestamps and capture-specific reviews remain retained. Academy\ncaptures prove the stated palette/focus/portal scope, not new responsiveness of\nits unchanged guest reader layout. No complete native/Rust suite is repeated\nmerely for commits, review attempts, helper/test edits or new source fingerprints.\n\n## Next and separate lanes\n\nSeal fresh qualification03 from the completed, bound observations and focused\nsource selectors. Run fresh independent member reviews and then the P11 phase\nreview against that one updated qualified candidate. Preserve all earlier\nscores and outcomes. No final P11 standing or production publication is claimed\nyet; `controller_complete` remains false.\n\nThe Linux branch's focused typecheck and 77/77 DOM tests retain their recorded\nsource/platform scope. They are macOS-hosted integration checks, not Linux native,\nAppImage or installed acceptance. Linux qualification remains independent.\nStable installed/live C26 acceptance remains deferred by the owner. After P11\nacceptance, use the reviewed source pin for the approved builder and a new\nimmutable production candidate; preserve RC1. Signing readiness on Jadzia is\nunverified.\n\nNo real tenant API calls, remote IAM changes, owner credential-value reads,\nhistorical seal edits or RC1 asset changes are claimed for these refinements.\n .gitattributes                                     |     7 +\n AGENTS.md               