y ad-hoc trust append is a separate admission-condition change, not a production code change; the successful current recovery reads the existing key. These retained native observations still belong to their original application and execution conditions.\",\n    \"C46-N02\": \"Production OAuth admission, setup verification, warnings, Inbox and endpoint authorities are unchanged. The two Rust fixture edits authenticate existing synthetic integration consumers; the production frontend delta is confined to API collection recovery. Retain the original native observation and artifact; relevant helper bytes and conservative production/resource dependencies are unchanged. The recorded fixture-only ad-hoc trust append is a separate admission-condition change, not a production code change; the successful current recovery reads the existing key. These retained native observations still belong to their original application and execution conditions.\",\n    \"C46-N03\": \"Production OAuth admission, setup verification, warnings, Inbox and endpoint authorities are unchanged. The two Rust fixture edits authenticate existing synthetic integration consumers; the production frontend delta is confined to API collection recovery. Retain the original native observation and artifact; relevant helper bytes and conservative production/resource dependencies are unchanged. The recorded fixture-only ad-hoc trust append is a separate admission-condition change, not a production code change; the successful current recovery reads the existing key. These retained native observations still belong to their original application and execution conditions.\",\n    \"C47-N01\": \"Shell/page hierarchy, Explain rendering/interaction, navigation, icons, focus and CSS are unchanged. The added App snapshot call mutates only separately scoped API recovery state; it does not change the existing shell scope action or rendering. C47-N02 additionally binds the actual original-artifact independent-scroll supplemen